WEBVTT

00:40.830 --> 00:41.540
Too bad.

00:41.830 --> 00:42.520
Yeah.

00:42.700 --> 00:43.540
Sorry.

00:44.200 --> 00:45.710
Maybe next time.

00:46.130 --> 00:46.670
OK.

00:47.960 --> 00:48.960
Bye-bye.

00:49.130 --> 00:50.210
Bye-bye.

00:52.860 --> 00:54.810
It was a gigantic snail!

00:54.970 --> 00:56.510
There's no such thing.

01:03.720 --> 01:04.860
Delivery.

01:06.500 --> 01:07.920
TANAKA

01:15.870 --> 01:17.700
Should I open it?

01:18.930 --> 01:20.430
Shin... do?

01:29.020 --> 01:30.420
TO ASUKA

01:36.180 --> 01:37.220
It's beautiful.

01:55.370 --> 01:57.700
Oh, it's a...

01:59.200 --> 02:01.370
eupho... nium.

02:10.750 --> 02:12.460
Euphonium!

02:15.360 --> 02:18.110
TO ASUKA

02:21.780 --> 02:23.530
KANSAI CONCERT BAND COMPETITION

02:23.930 --> 02:26.730
Any words from the club president?

02:27.940 --> 02:28.810
Sensei!

02:28.980 --> 02:30.210
Yes, Tanaka-san?

02:31.270 --> 02:32.770
Before the president speaks,

02:35.570 --> 02:38.070
I'd like to express how I feel right now.

02:38.820 --> 02:40.570
I don't want to lose.

02:43.070 --> 02:46.750
I don't want this to end with,
"I'm glad we made it this far."

02:47.250 --> 02:50.690
Because we made it this far,
I want to advance.

02:50.920 --> 02:53.330
I want Kitauji's sound
to resonate all over Japan!

02:54.080 --> 02:57.680
We've practiced hard to get to this point.

02:58.090 --> 02:59.320
Let's give it our all!

03:00.820 --> 03:01.590
Yes!

04:34.460 --> 04:38.420
KANSAI CONCERT BAND
NATIONAL COMPETITION PRELIMINARIES

06:33.530 --> 06:38.560
SOUND! EUPHONIUM: THE MOVIE
MAY THE MELODY REACH YOU!

06:56.500 --> 06:57.500
Kumiko!

06:59.000 --> 07:00.420
There you are.

07:00.830 --> 07:01.520
We're on!

07:02.040 --> 07:04.040
Oh! OK.

07:05.230 --> 07:06.930
You always disappear.

07:07.340 --> 07:10.090
You make me sound like a kid.

07:10.380 --> 07:11.760
But you are childish.

07:11.930 --> 07:14.090
And you're so mature.

07:14.260 --> 07:15.730
You're annoying.

07:17.600 --> 07:21.270
Welcome to the Kitauji High School
Concert Band performance.

07:22.020 --> 07:24.690
At the recent
Kansai Concert Band Competition...

07:24.850 --> 07:25.860
Over there.

07:27.280 --> 07:28.700
See you later.

07:29.530 --> 07:31.260
- It's almost time.
- Yeah.

07:31.610 --> 07:33.280
I'm getting nervous.

07:39.540 --> 07:41.690
Kumiko Oumae.

07:43.370 --> 07:45.050
Asuka-senpai!

07:45.420 --> 07:48.220
You were late. Where were you,
the bathroom?

07:48.380 --> 07:49.230
Yeah...

07:49.470 --> 07:51.380
What? What are you nervous?

07:51.550 --> 07:52.860
A little...

07:52.860 --> 07:56.640
How cute! Still a freshman after all.

07:57.270 --> 08:02.100
I'm not playing the euphonium today,
so I'm counting on you and Natsuki.

08:02.870 --> 08:03.640
Yes!

08:03.890 --> 08:04.730
All right!

08:06.280 --> 08:08.740
Senpai, you look happy.

08:09.740 --> 08:13.760
Why wouldn't I be?
We're going to Nationals!

08:14.570 --> 08:15.620
Right.

08:16.620 --> 08:19.830
You really love the concert band.

08:21.410 --> 08:22.750
Do I really?

08:23.660 --> 08:24.250
Huh?

08:25.090 --> 08:27.270
Oumae-chan, do you like the euphonium?

08:27.590 --> 08:30.130
Huh? Well...

08:30.590 --> 08:35.180
No one's ever asked me that before.
It's a bit intimidating.

08:35.350 --> 08:37.600
I do. I love it.

08:40.100 --> 08:43.100
I don't really care about the competition.

08:47.360 --> 08:48.110
Just kidding.

08:49.480 --> 08:50.610
Asuka!

08:51.110 --> 08:52.150
Coming!

08:52.480 --> 08:55.120
Let's enjoy the school festival!

08:55.620 --> 08:57.290
Y-yeah...

09:00.160 --> 09:00.870
I'm counting on you.

09:01.450 --> 09:02.790
Leave it to me!

09:08.630 --> 09:12.500
Our concert band has thrived
thanks to the support

09:12.710 --> 09:16.680
of our teachers, parents,
and countless others.

09:16.850 --> 09:18.640
Thank you very much.

09:21.890 --> 09:27.320
The National Concert Band Competition
is held at the end of October in Nagoya.

09:30.570 --> 09:36.430
We'll practice hard so we can
bring you good news from Nagoya!

09:36.990 --> 09:40.470
Please sit back and enjoy
"School Paradise."

09:48.000 --> 09:50.040
<i>Our fledgling Kitauji High School
Concert band...</i>

09:50.210 --> 09:51.840
KITAUJI HIGH SCHOOL FESTIVAL CONCERT BAND

09:52.000 --> 09:55.000
<i>...got a new advisor this spring,</i>

09:55.220 --> 09:57.100
<i>who is Taki-Sensei.</i>

09:58.030 --> 10:01.720
<i>Together, we made it
to the National competition.</i>

10:09.380 --> 10:11.880
NATIONAL CONCERT BAND COMPETITION

10:13.630 --> 10:14.560
Good job.

10:15.200 --> 10:16.950
You too.

10:17.120 --> 10:18.370
I saw your mom.

10:18.530 --> 10:20.240
Oh, I didn't notice.

10:20.410 --> 10:21.950
She might come to your class.

10:23.410 --> 10:24.450
What a nice couple.

10:24.620 --> 10:27.630
Natsuki-senpai! Please don't.

10:28.710 --> 10:31.380
It's been a while since
we performed together.

10:31.540 --> 10:33.210
Since Sunfest?

10:33.540 --> 10:35.970
Right? It's so much fun.

10:36.930 --> 10:38.760
OK! Winds, move it.

10:40.220 --> 10:43.260
Clean up your area before you leave.

10:43.590 --> 10:47.560
We'll move the big instruments later.
Guys, please help out.

10:47.770 --> 10:48.440
Yes!

10:48.980 --> 10:49.980
And...

10:53.150 --> 10:57.110
It's a busy season.
Don't burn yourselves out.

10:57.490 --> 11:01.910
Intense practices for Nationals
will be starting soon!

11:02.780 --> 11:03.610
Understood?

11:03.780 --> 11:04.410
Yes!

11:04.570 --> 11:05.160
Good!

11:05.430 --> 11:06.620
WE LOVE THE CONCERT BAND!

11:06.830 --> 11:09.790
Asuka-senpai sure is amazing.

11:10.250 --> 11:13.920
I was waiting for her to say,
"Stay focused!"

11:14.080 --> 11:14.920
Right?

11:15.170 --> 11:18.470
Feels like she can reach
the moon. She's so cool!

11:19.300 --> 11:21.590
OK! Let's have fun!

11:21.820 --> 11:22.590
MUSIC ROOM

11:22.760 --> 11:24.090
Reina, what are you doing after?

11:24.260 --> 11:25.640
I haven't decided yet.

11:25.810 --> 11:27.190
Then come to our class!

11:27.350 --> 11:28.940
- Yeah, come!
- It'll be fun!

11:29.270 --> 11:31.270
I'm really glad to back!

11:31.600 --> 11:32.520
That's good.

11:32.940 --> 11:35.650
I'll do my best to support Kitauji!

11:37.110 --> 11:38.650
I'm counting on you.

11:38.840 --> 11:39.820
Yes!

11:41.610 --> 11:43.780
OK, then. Let's clean up.

11:50.710 --> 11:53.620
I don't really care about the competition.

11:54.500 --> 11:55.380
Asuka!

11:55.630 --> 11:57.130
What are you doing now?

11:58.800 --> 12:00.300
<i>Asuka Tanaka.</i>

12:01.050 --> 12:03.970
<i>Leader of the bass section
and vice president of the club.</i>

12:04.800 --> 12:08.480
<i>A senior that everyone in the band
loves and relies on.</i>

12:09.310 --> 12:12.390
<i>But today, I saw a cold expression
on her face.</i>

12:13.310 --> 12:16.990
<i>Then it disappeared like a mirage.</i>

12:19.150 --> 12:20.240
<i>It made me wonder</i>

12:21.320 --> 12:24.690
<i>what Asuka-senpai was
seeing that I wasn't.</i>

12:24.990 --> 12:26.000
Kumiko-chan?

12:26.540 --> 12:27.910
Let's clean up soon?

12:28.080 --> 12:29.370
Oh, sorry.

12:31.330 --> 12:35.160
<i>But I was scared to think about it.</i>

12:42.190 --> 12:43.760
NATIONAL CONCERT BAND COMPETITION

12:49.930 --> 12:50.850
I'm home!

13:01.360 --> 13:02.360
Welcome home.

13:02.690 --> 13:05.580
Thanks, sorry I came home so late.

13:06.410 --> 13:08.220
- Stew tonight?
- Yeah.

13:09.120 --> 13:10.700
Hey, Mom?

13:11.040 --> 13:13.870
Hm? Looks delicious. What is it?

13:14.870 --> 13:18.630
By the way Asuka,
about your college entrance exams.

13:19.050 --> 13:22.050
I'm counting on you to do your best.

13:23.300 --> 13:23.920
Yeah.

13:25.300 --> 13:26.430
Sorry, you were saying?

13:27.890 --> 13:30.470
Nothing, never mind.

13:38.920 --> 13:39.920
MUSIC ROOM

13:42.440 --> 13:47.120
Good. The fortissimo from "L"
should sound crystal clear.

13:47.510 --> 13:48.340
Yes!

13:48.620 --> 13:51.780
Snare drum, keep your rolls sharp.

13:52.120 --> 13:52.740
Yes!

13:53.240 --> 13:56.350
OK, let's call it a day.

13:57.420 --> 14:00.130
Now that the school festival is over,
make sure to get plenty of rest.

14:01.630 --> 14:03.840
The concert camp is this week.

14:04.420 --> 14:08.430
I want everyone to be
in good physical condition.

14:08.950 --> 14:09.570
Yes!

14:12.100 --> 14:13.640
Don't catch a cold.

14:14.640 --> 14:15.410
Yes.

14:15.650 --> 14:18.150
We need to go over the itinerary.

14:18.310 --> 14:21.360
Section leaders,
let's meet in the classroom.

14:28.700 --> 14:29.780
Kumiko-chan!

14:30.660 --> 14:31.870
Let's go home together.

14:32.030 --> 14:33.120
Sure.

14:35.160 --> 14:39.630
<i>That conversation with Asuka-senpai at
the school festival was bothering me.</i>

14:41.500 --> 14:43.880
<i>Was that really a joke?</i>

14:45.170 --> 14:49.970
<i>If that's how she really felt,
I would feel betrayed.</i>

14:52.050 --> 14:55.300
<i>I hated myself for even thinking that.</i>

14:57.690 --> 14:58.960
I'm home.

15:01.520 --> 15:02.810
Oh, you're home!

15:03.690 --> 15:05.190
Oh, Dad's here.

15:05.350 --> 15:06.740
He leaves early tomorrow.

15:08.360 --> 15:09.360
Here, Dad.

15:10.320 --> 15:15.200
Oh, that's right. I called Mamiko today.
She was shocked you made it to Nationals.

15:15.540 --> 15:16.870
She wishes you luck.

15:21.870 --> 15:25.170
Kumiko, you're enjoying the band,
but are you studying too?

15:25.330 --> 15:27.430
Yeah, here and there.

15:28.220 --> 15:29.550
What's that mean?

15:30.090 --> 15:33.840
Mamiko quit music to focus
on studying at your age.

15:34.180 --> 15:35.520
You should too.

15:36.020 --> 15:37.190
Yeah, yeah.

15:37.730 --> 15:39.350
Isn't my older sister is amazing?

15:39.520 --> 15:41.330
Don't be sarcastic.

15:41.850 --> 15:43.100
So annoying...

15:43.390 --> 15:45.570
Dinner is ready.

15:52.090 --> 15:54.050
You're quitting trombone?

15:54.950 --> 15:56.910
What's it to you?

15:58.430 --> 15:59.410
Whatever.

16:04.540 --> 16:06.090
<i>I need to focus.</i>

16:06.760 --> 16:11.920
There's no time to breathe
so I end up rushing it.

16:12.550 --> 16:14.030
Try to stagger it?

16:14.420 --> 16:16.560
Goto, when do you take a breath?

16:17.230 --> 16:18.120
Here.

16:19.640 --> 16:23.100
Then Goto should take a
breath two bars later.

16:23.770 --> 16:27.610
That way, Riko-chan won't have to
finish this phrase in one breath.

16:27.900 --> 16:28.960
Got it.

16:29.280 --> 16:30.920
How about the contrabass?

16:31.240 --> 16:33.490
Sapphire Kawashima is perfect!

16:33.650 --> 16:35.240
It's Midori!

16:35.830 --> 16:39.660
- Let's play it again.
- Excuse me.

16:39.850 --> 16:40.770
But first...

16:42.080 --> 16:46.730
Kumiko Oumae! Your mind is elsewhere.
What's wrong?

16:48.300 --> 16:52.070
You can tell me. I'll take care of it!

16:52.260 --> 16:54.090
I'm sure you will.

16:54.410 --> 16:55.810
Just tell me!

16:55.970 --> 16:57.070
Ow!

16:57.930 --> 17:03.680
<i>It was time for our three-day camp
in the lingering heat of summer.</i>

17:06.330 --> 17:06.940
STUDY ROOM 1

17:07.110 --> 17:08.340
Breathing first!

17:12.820 --> 17:14.650
Take a deep breath, then blow.

17:14.820 --> 17:18.700
<i>We did breathing and voice
exercises in the morning.</i>

17:20.390 --> 17:23.180
<i>Then we practiced
in our respective sections.</i>

17:23.620 --> 17:26.690
<i>The afternoons were dedicated
to ensemble practice.</i>

17:27.460 --> 17:29.670
Let's do a "tenner."

17:29.960 --> 17:30.630
Yes!

17:35.560 --> 17:39.010
<i>A "tenner" is practicing
our compulsory piece</i>

17:39.280 --> 17:42.640
<i>and free piece ten times in a row.</i>

17:43.970 --> 17:46.070
<i>Two pieces run around 12 minutes.</i>

17:46.790 --> 17:49.040
<i>We rest for two minutes in between.</i>

17:49.570 --> 17:51.690
<i>So the whole exercise
takes over 160 minutes.</i>

17:52.520 --> 17:54.860
<i>By the end, we're all...</i>

17:55.320 --> 17:56.240
<i>...like this.</i>

17:57.200 --> 17:59.410
Let's take a twenty minute break.

18:01.160 --> 18:04.330
Twenty minutes? I think I'll go play.

18:05.490 --> 18:06.670
Wow...

18:18.510 --> 18:19.850
OK, stop.

18:21.890 --> 18:22.620
Euphoniums.

18:22.890 --> 18:23.510
Yes!

18:24.180 --> 18:26.940
You've gotten much better
since the Kansai tournament.

18:27.900 --> 18:30.400
Oumae-san, your sound is more stable.

18:31.360 --> 18:33.110
Don't forget how that feels.

18:34.190 --> 18:34.730
Yes!

18:37.530 --> 18:38.450
Good for you!

18:40.740 --> 18:41.370
Thanks.

18:43.200 --> 18:46.630
This is the last year for the seniors.

18:47.040 --> 18:47.630
Yeah.

18:48.290 --> 18:53.290
It's hard to imagine
they won't be here next year.

18:54.380 --> 18:59.150
Haruka-senpai, Kaori-senpai,
and Asuka-senpai...

19:01.890 --> 19:04.660
Reina, do you like the trumpet?

19:05.050 --> 19:06.400
Of course I do.

19:08.560 --> 19:09.730
Why do you ask?

19:11.600 --> 19:14.150
Asuka-senpai asked me the same thing.

19:14.940 --> 19:16.280
What did you say?

19:17.240 --> 19:21.950
That it's intimidating or something...

19:23.160 --> 19:24.570
Sounds like you.

19:34.250 --> 19:37.430
I should have brought my pillow after all.

19:41.760 --> 19:42.930
So beautiful...

19:49.310 --> 19:50.440
A euphonium?

20:14.160 --> 20:15.620
Asuka-senpai.

20:35.390 --> 20:40.490
<i>The piece was mysterious, warm
and sad, all at the same time.</i>

20:41.490 --> 20:44.900
<i>As if those emotions were
layered on top of each other.</i>

21:04.050 --> 21:05.010
OK, everyone.

21:05.510 --> 21:10.350
We'll practice as an ensemble
on the days that are circled.

21:11.100 --> 21:12.020
OK?

21:12.180 --> 21:12.850
Yes!

21:13.100 --> 21:15.020
That's it for today.

21:15.350 --> 21:16.940
Thank you.

21:19.440 --> 21:21.110
Station Building Concert...

21:21.940 --> 21:24.780
In the atrium, right?

21:25.070 --> 21:29.040
Why are we even doing it with Nationals
just around the corner?

21:29.200 --> 21:32.450
Some thought we should
prioritize the competition,

21:32.620 --> 21:36.210
Taki-Sensei said that performing
experience is valuable.

21:36.380 --> 21:38.960
I've never played at
a venue like this before.

21:39.130 --> 21:40.050
I'm looking forward to it.

21:40.210 --> 21:40.960
Me, too!

21:47.560 --> 21:49.660
You're in a good mood, Hazuki-chan.

21:50.060 --> 21:50.640
I guess.

21:52.060 --> 21:55.390
I love performing with everyone.

21:55.560 --> 21:57.440
Hey, where's Kumiko-chan?

21:57.820 --> 22:01.820
She went to take our notebooks
to the teacher's office.

22:02.230 --> 22:03.230
Excuse me...

22:03.400 --> 22:05.400
What do you intend to do about it?

22:06.490 --> 22:07.280
I'm sorry.

22:07.450 --> 22:11.280
Why are you apologizing?
They need to apologize to us!

22:11.910 --> 22:13.910
Please don't yell, Mom.

22:14.990 --> 22:19.250
As a teacher, you should know what
they need to focus on right now.

22:19.960 --> 22:24.960
She's not getting a music scholarship.
She needs to study for college exams!

22:25.590 --> 22:27.970
Y-you're absolutely right.

22:28.200 --> 22:31.350
Then let her quit the concert band!

22:31.930 --> 22:37.770
But this year's band is doing so well.
They've qualified for Nationals and--

22:37.940 --> 22:42.690
I have no intention of accepting
her letter of resignation.

22:44.090 --> 22:48.160
Did you force her to write it?

22:50.320 --> 22:52.950
And what if I did?

22:53.530 --> 22:56.560
I raised my daughter on my own.

22:57.130 --> 22:59.060
Without any help! By myself!

22:59.500 --> 23:02.310
So I will determine her future!

23:02.960 --> 23:05.630
Concert band is holding her back!

23:06.390 --> 23:09.890
I-I understand how you feel, but...

23:10.050 --> 23:12.660
I'll honor Asuka's wishes.

23:13.180 --> 23:16.500
If she doesn't want to quit,
I won't accept the letter.

23:16.810 --> 23:17.850
No matter what.

23:18.810 --> 23:22.810
Asuka is doing a great job
as vice president of the band.

23:23.480 --> 23:26.840
They're fulfilling their dream
of competing at Nationals.

23:27.740 --> 23:30.320
Why can't you support her?

23:41.000 --> 23:44.330
Asuka, tell them
you're quitting right now.

23:46.180 --> 23:48.860
Say it. You're quitting.

23:51.590 --> 23:54.340
Mom, I don't want to--

24:04.060 --> 24:06.170
Why can't you listen to me?

24:06.400 --> 24:07.670
Ms. Tanaka...

24:07.860 --> 24:11.050
You're playing that instrument
to get back at me!

24:11.450 --> 24:13.450
Do you want to make me suffer?

24:18.580 --> 24:19.870
Asuka...

24:20.750 --> 24:24.870
Asuka, I'm sorry... I did it again.

24:25.540 --> 24:26.590
I lost my temper.

24:30.470 --> 24:31.450
It's fine.

24:33.260 --> 24:34.300
I'm sorry.

24:35.050 --> 24:38.810
I'm sorry, Taki-Sensei.
I'm going to take my mother home.

24:39.140 --> 24:40.890
May I skip practice today?

24:42.390 --> 24:43.370
That's fine.

24:45.930 --> 24:48.250
Let's go, Mom.

25:04.790 --> 25:07.670
<i>Word of this incident
spread like wildfire.</i>

25:08.270 --> 25:11.130
<i>The concert band was shaken.</i>

25:13.630 --> 25:17.100
Is Asuka-senpai really quitting?

25:18.310 --> 25:22.310
I don't know. Why was she so angry?

25:23.430 --> 25:25.100
Her mother?

25:27.030 --> 25:29.880
Club activities should be our choice.

25:30.320 --> 25:34.940
College exams and careers
should be our choice too.

25:35.860 --> 25:39.700
I'm sure she's worried about Asuka, but...

25:45.200 --> 25:46.300
What's wrong?

25:48.960 --> 25:52.550
But why is Asuka-senpai
insisting on playing?

25:53.130 --> 25:57.560
Seniors have college exams
and her mom is so against it.

25:58.060 --> 26:00.780
Because she loves the band?

26:00.970 --> 26:04.970
Really? I don't get
that impression from her.

26:05.350 --> 26:09.400
Sometimes I feel like
she's just playing for herself.

26:17.830 --> 26:20.910
I don't understand her.

26:22.240 --> 26:23.470
<i>But the next day,</i>

26:24.080 --> 26:28.090
<i>as if to laugh off all
our worries, Asuka-senpai...</i>

26:28.250 --> 26:30.670
Looking good!

26:31.480 --> 26:32.880
<i>...just reappeared.</i>

26:33.230 --> 26:35.210
Asuka-senpai!

26:35.380 --> 26:36.390
Senpai!

26:37.600 --> 26:39.350
What's up, everyone?

26:39.510 --> 26:42.930
Haruka-senpai said you didn't
come to school today.

26:43.600 --> 26:46.400
You're not quitting, are you?
You'll keep playing?

26:48.940 --> 26:52.190
You're bombarding me with questions!

26:52.360 --> 26:53.730
Senpai...

26:55.060 --> 26:56.570
Why are you crying?

26:56.870 --> 26:57.800
Because...

26:58.030 --> 27:01.620
Come on, Goto! Console your girlfriend.

27:03.530 --> 27:07.710
I see. So word got around.

27:08.080 --> 27:12.940
Sorry, everyone. Sorry, Oumae-chan.
You must have been shocked.

27:13.540 --> 27:15.960
No! Asuka-senpai...

27:16.430 --> 27:20.530
Don't worry! I won't let you guys down.

27:21.550 --> 27:22.800
Thank goodness!

27:22.970 --> 27:26.310
I told you it would be all right!

27:26.980 --> 27:31.770
OK, enough of that! Let's practice!

27:31.940 --> 27:32.730
Yes!

27:33.060 --> 27:35.770
I was worried for a moment.

27:35.940 --> 27:36.610
Natsuki.

27:39.570 --> 27:42.160
Can we talk later?

27:43.240 --> 27:43.950
Yeah.

27:44.720 --> 27:50.060
Everything's fine! Don't worry so much!

27:51.080 --> 27:51.670
Really?

27:52.290 --> 27:54.420
Re-a-lly.

27:55.080 --> 27:59.090
You guys are so serious.
It's not that big of a deal.

27:59.300 --> 27:59.930
Liar.

28:01.010 --> 28:03.930
Your mom called the school today.

28:04.130 --> 28:06.440
I heard the headmaster
and Taki-Sensi talking.

28:10.310 --> 28:11.600
I see.

28:14.190 --> 28:15.440
What's really going on?

28:16.490 --> 28:18.860
Talk to us. We'll try to help...

28:19.030 --> 28:20.110
It's fine.

28:20.860 --> 28:22.650
I won't let you guys down.

28:23.860 --> 28:27.770
Isn't that enough?
The performance is the top priority.

28:28.120 --> 28:29.160
That's all.

28:29.790 --> 28:31.120
That's all...?

28:31.350 --> 28:34.000
Yeah, that's all. It's a club activity.

28:35.210 --> 28:36.040
So...

28:37.630 --> 28:39.630
Stop obsessing over it, OK?

28:40.510 --> 28:43.510
Please be... quiet.

28:44.170 --> 28:45.070
Asuka.

28:49.810 --> 28:54.810
<i>From the following day,
Asuka-senpai stopped coming.</i>

28:56.820 --> 28:59.130
Asuka-senpai's not here again?

28:59.130 --> 29:02.150
Huh? Oh, yeah...

29:02.650 --> 29:03.590
Has she called?

29:05.070 --> 29:09.160
We can't focus on that right now.
Let's focus on practicing.

29:09.330 --> 29:10.830
NATIONALS, HERE WE COME!

29:12.540 --> 29:13.660
Have you heard from her?

29:14.330 --> 29:18.210
No. I've been texting her every day.

29:18.840 --> 29:20.010
How about you, Kaori?

29:20.550 --> 29:23.320
No... What's that?

29:24.010 --> 29:27.060
Asuka's sheet music. I found it.

29:27.850 --> 29:30.680
She probably can't take it home.

29:31.850 --> 29:32.680
Asuka's...

29:35.710 --> 29:37.210
TO NATIONALS!

29:41.230 --> 29:42.440
Kaori-senpai!

29:43.530 --> 29:47.700
The headmaster accepted
Asuka-senpai's letter of resignation!

30:00.960 --> 30:05.300
What's going on? Are you all losing focus?

30:08.600 --> 30:09.310
Um...

30:10.060 --> 30:10.760
What is it?

30:12.600 --> 30:14.600
Asuka-senpai's resignation letter.

30:14.890 --> 30:18.940
Did the headmaster
accept it on your behalf?

30:21.820 --> 30:23.800
There's no truth to that.

30:26.630 --> 30:30.580
So every time you hear a rumor,

30:30.850 --> 30:34.910
you're going to lose focus
and play like amateurs?

30:36.630 --> 30:39.520
Let's call it a day.
Practice in your own sections.

30:40.960 --> 30:41.860
Sensei!

30:47.780 --> 30:49.030
NATIONALS!!!

30:52.430 --> 30:53.370
TO NATIONALS!

31:00.610 --> 31:03.440
Listen, everyone.

31:04.310 --> 31:05.110
Haruka...

31:06.270 --> 31:09.530
I know everyone is feeling
anxious with Asuka gone.

31:10.660 --> 31:14.120
But we have to stop relying on her.

31:14.950 --> 31:18.630
We can't let anxiety take over
and affect our performance.

31:19.460 --> 31:20.900
We're better than that.

31:21.330 --> 31:22.820
We know that.

31:23.000 --> 31:23.710
But...

31:25.500 --> 31:29.550
I know Asuka is more capable than me.

31:30.390 --> 31:34.390
I always thought she'd
make a better president.

31:36.010 --> 31:40.290
We all depended on her
because she can do anything.

31:41.310 --> 31:44.980
We thought it was okay
because Asuka is special.

31:46.490 --> 31:49.660
But she wasn't special.

31:50.570 --> 31:53.990
We just put her on a pedestal.

31:55.320 --> 31:58.040
Vice president, section leader,
drum major...

31:58.500 --> 32:01.000
<i>We expected her to do it all perfectly.</i>

32:01.580 --> 32:05.500
She never showed any vulnerability,
so we assumed she was okay.

32:09.720 --> 32:12.720
But now it's our turn to support Asuka.

32:13.510 --> 32:15.840
So she can return at any time.

32:19.940 --> 32:21.730
Please...

32:23.730 --> 32:25.390
Don't underestimate us.

32:26.700 --> 32:30.700
You don't need to tell us.
We'll follow your lead!

32:31.700 --> 32:33.950
We're all serious, you know.

32:46.210 --> 32:50.420
<i>The day of the station building
concert finally arrived.</i>

32:52.550 --> 32:53.860
I'm getting nervous.

32:54.220 --> 32:55.130
I hope we can do this.

32:55.300 --> 32:57.390
You'll be fine, Hazuki-chan!

32:57.560 --> 32:58.560
But...

32:59.310 --> 33:00.390
Seira High...

33:01.000 --> 33:04.890
They seem so confident.
They go to Nationals every year.

33:05.890 --> 33:09.110
But we're going to Nationals too.

33:11.780 --> 33:12.720
That's right.

33:12.900 --> 33:14.610
Yeah, that's right!

33:15.550 --> 33:16.400
Asuka!

33:17.250 --> 33:20.410
What? It's like you've seen a ghost.

33:20.790 --> 33:21.830
Asuka-senpai.

33:22.620 --> 33:23.450
You came.

33:23.620 --> 33:26.250
I told you I wouldn't let you down.

33:26.410 --> 33:27.340
Asuka-senpai!

33:27.510 --> 33:28.630
Senpai!

33:29.800 --> 33:31.920
We were so worried!

33:32.760 --> 33:34.820
Don't cry again.

33:35.420 --> 33:36.010
Asuka.

33:38.140 --> 33:40.680
I'm playing the solo.

33:41.770 --> 33:43.180
So support me, OK?

33:48.280 --> 33:49.320
Of course!

38:20.710 --> 38:22.420
This is too much to cover...

38:22.750 --> 38:26.210
I told you I was serious
from the beginning!

38:27.100 --> 38:29.390
But you're graduating next year.

38:29.640 --> 38:32.930
It'll be too late by then!
I have to do this now!

38:33.580 --> 38:36.940
But... why beauty school?

38:39.730 --> 38:42.570
I've always done what you wanted.

38:43.570 --> 38:47.240
As the older sister,
I've endured everything.

38:48.660 --> 38:49.240
Mamiko.

38:50.120 --> 38:55.080
I never wanted to switch schools
or study for college entrance exams!

38:55.780 --> 38:59.130
I wanted to play music, like Kumiko!

38:59.590 --> 39:01.750
I didn't want to quit the trombone!

39:02.420 --> 39:06.930
Then you should have said so
before you started college.

39:08.600 --> 39:11.030
You made that impossible.

39:14.140 --> 39:18.480
Your mom and I may have
expected a lot from you.

39:19.150 --> 39:23.310
But it was your decision to go to college.

39:25.020 --> 39:27.450
If you're going to quit now, then get out.

39:28.320 --> 39:31.780
Take care of your own living expenses
and beauty school tuition.

39:32.280 --> 39:32.870
All right?

39:33.870 --> 39:35.780
Wait, Dad...

39:36.320 --> 39:37.960
Show me you mean it.

39:46.630 --> 39:49.220
You're quitting college?

39:50.340 --> 39:54.470
After you got after me to study?
You're quitting?

39:55.220 --> 40:00.230
Why? I thought you wanted to get into
a good college and find a good job!

40:00.730 --> 40:02.230
It'll all be for nothing!

40:04.190 --> 40:05.690
Stay out of it.

40:08.410 --> 40:10.660
Why did you quit the trombone?

40:10.820 --> 40:11.700
Whatever.

40:11.860 --> 40:14.700
I want to play with you.

40:14.860 --> 40:15.930
Shut up.

40:15.930 --> 40:17.870
Mamiko...

40:18.870 --> 40:20.770
I told you to shut up!

40:21.000 --> 40:23.770
Shut up or I'll sew your mouth shut!

40:34.380 --> 40:36.380
Is Mamiko dropping out of college?

40:36.880 --> 40:38.020
How did you know?

40:38.350 --> 40:40.560
My mom heard.

40:41.520 --> 40:43.520
She told me not to tell anyone.

40:44.230 --> 40:46.020
Did something happen at school?

40:46.850 --> 40:51.570
No idea. We don't talk much
since she started college.

40:52.890 --> 40:54.890
MUSIC ROOM

40:59.580 --> 41:01.140
OK, Number 13.

41:01.540 --> 41:03.710
Asuka Tanaka is back!

41:04.250 --> 41:05.540
Give me a break.

41:06.580 --> 41:09.720
<i>After the station building concert,
Asuka-senpai</i>

41:09.880 --> 41:13.590
<i>rarely came to practice, even with
the competition coming up.</i>

41:13.910 --> 41:15.880
We were all worried.

41:16.050 --> 41:18.200
You even ignored our texts.

41:18.430 --> 41:21.810
I told you. I won't let you guys down.

41:21.980 --> 41:22.890
But...

41:23.140 --> 41:25.270
OK, take your seats everyone.

41:26.140 --> 41:28.070
Morning! How's it going?

41:28.280 --> 41:29.460
Slowly.

41:29.900 --> 41:32.970
You never change, Oumae-chan.

41:32.970 --> 41:34.470
What do you mean?

41:35.280 --> 41:36.900
It's a compliment, actually.

41:37.580 --> 41:39.660
<i>She was back to her old self.</i>

41:40.500 --> 41:43.500
<i>But when I saw that
cold profile of hers again,</i>

41:43.850 --> 41:46.330
<i>I was overcome with anxiety.</i>

41:48.800 --> 41:49.480
Um...

41:51.300 --> 41:54.760
You're not quitting are you, Asuka-senpai?

41:56.800 --> 41:58.600
Are you?

41:59.990 --> 42:00.930
You're not--

42:01.160 --> 42:04.520
Shut up, or I'll sew your mouth shut.

42:06.680 --> 42:09.840
By the way, aren't mid-terms coming up?

42:10.190 --> 42:14.610
You said high school subjects
were a lot harder.

42:15.480 --> 42:18.160
Well, math is a lot harder.

42:18.330 --> 42:19.490
Want some help?

42:20.330 --> 42:25.850
Practices end early next week, right?
Why don't you come over?

42:26.950 --> 42:29.840
To your house?

42:35.800 --> 42:36.670
Mamiko.

42:38.470 --> 42:39.560
Shuichi?

42:39.970 --> 42:41.970
It's been a while.

42:42.470 --> 42:46.510
You grew. And you look cool!
You must be popular.

42:47.230 --> 42:48.480
Not really...

42:49.730 --> 42:50.360
See ya.

42:52.360 --> 42:52.980
Um...

42:55.150 --> 42:59.970
Have you ever heard us play, Mamiko?

43:00.160 --> 43:00.830
Why?

43:01.330 --> 43:03.330
It would be nice if you did.

43:03.990 --> 43:08.000
We performed well at Kansai.
We even shocked ourselves.

43:08.670 --> 43:10.380
And we're going to Nationals.

43:10.980 --> 43:12.880
So I should go to Nagoya?

43:13.340 --> 43:15.380
I know... it's far.

43:18.180 --> 43:23.680
But I think Kumiko would like you
to hear her play, just once.

43:24.510 --> 43:28.360
She started playing in the
concert band because of you.

43:30.020 --> 43:31.110
Because of me?

43:32.690 --> 43:33.610
Now?

43:35.020 --> 43:35.900
Just a little.

43:36.060 --> 43:37.740
It's too loud.

43:43.200 --> 43:44.280
You'll play for me?

43:47.290 --> 43:48.390
Mamiko...

44:02.220 --> 44:03.220
I'd forgotten.

44:05.050 --> 44:08.270
We'll end practice here today.

44:09.100 --> 44:11.400
I have something to tell you.

44:12.940 --> 44:15.060
If I don't get confirmation
by this weekend

44:15.400 --> 44:18.740
that Asuka is going to continue
in the concert band,

44:19.820 --> 44:24.010
Nakagawa-san will take her place
at the National competition.

44:35.290 --> 44:36.250
Oumae-chan.

44:38.090 --> 44:39.430
Natsuki-senpai.

44:41.090 --> 44:44.280
Am I not good enough?

44:44.760 --> 44:48.020
No, it's not... like that.

44:48.440 --> 44:49.690
I'm scared.

44:52.620 --> 44:54.640
How long have you known?

44:56.190 --> 44:59.860
Since Asuka-senpai's mother
came to school.

45:01.030 --> 45:02.530
Asuka-senpai told me...

45:06.850 --> 45:08.100
CONSERVE POWER

45:10.830 --> 45:12.500
<i>Natsuki-senpai's sheet music</i>

45:13.290 --> 45:16.870
<i>was all marked up with
pointers from Asuka-senpai.</i>

45:18.610 --> 45:20.360
NATIONALS, HERE WE COME!

45:20.630 --> 45:22.300
<i>It was like reading a will.</i>

45:26.220 --> 45:27.310
Bring her back?

45:28.140 --> 45:33.020
You're going to her house
to study next week, right?

45:33.170 --> 45:33.960
I can't.

45:34.680 --> 45:36.560
I haven't said anything yet.

45:36.850 --> 45:40.320
You want me to convince her mom, right?

45:42.150 --> 45:42.990
Yeah.

45:43.150 --> 45:46.360
That's impossible! I can't!

45:46.600 --> 45:50.680
Don't worry. Kaori-senpai gave
me a secret weapon.

45:51.660 --> 45:53.580
Chestnut confectionaries...

45:53.750 --> 45:56.310
<i>...from Koufu-do. They're the best!</i>

45:56.870 --> 45:58.170
What is this?

45:58.880 --> 46:01.670
Asuka-senpai's mother's favorite.

46:02.380 --> 46:05.010
You can't lose with this.

46:05.380 --> 46:07.560
Look me in the eye and say it.

46:07.720 --> 46:08.680
OK...

46:11.560 --> 46:14.680
Even if I succeed in convincing her mom,

46:14.930 --> 46:18.690
you'll lose your place if
Asuka-senpai comes back.

46:19.900 --> 46:22.610
I don't mind. I have next year.

46:23.690 --> 46:28.120
Right now, it's better for the club
if Asuka-senpai comes back.

46:30.580 --> 46:33.200
Are you being honest with yourself?

46:36.870 --> 46:40.880
I knew you'd ask me that. Yes, I am.

46:47.600 --> 46:50.260
So that's what
you guys were talking about.

46:51.060 --> 46:53.200
It's a big responsibility.

46:54.760 --> 46:59.230
Reina, why do you think
Asuka-senpai invited me?

46:59.610 --> 47:04.730
I play in a different section,
so I don't know her that well.

47:04.900 --> 47:06.650
Yeah...

47:06.880 --> 47:08.840
MATH I

47:11.330 --> 47:12.080
There she is.

47:15.450 --> 47:16.580
Oumae-chan!

47:17.160 --> 47:19.290
Ah... what's that book?

47:19.630 --> 47:20.840
Wanna know?

47:21.150 --> 47:23.920
If it's good, I'll lend it to you.

47:25.420 --> 47:25.960
Let's go.

47:28.320 --> 47:28.970
OK.

47:30.930 --> 47:34.970
This is my house.
Don't worry, no one's home.

47:41.150 --> 47:42.650
Here you go.

47:43.750 --> 47:44.690
Thank you.

47:48.340 --> 47:49.160
Nervous?

47:49.320 --> 47:50.620
N-no.

47:51.700 --> 47:53.990
You brought your euphonium home.

47:55.950 --> 47:57.710
My mom doesn't know though.

47:59.210 --> 48:01.130
Oh... I see.

48:04.380 --> 48:06.540
OK, show me.

48:07.330 --> 48:08.140
Your notes.

48:10.300 --> 48:11.340
Here.

48:16.680 --> 48:17.520
Young lady!

48:18.480 --> 48:20.520
This is serious.

48:21.690 --> 48:22.480
Yeah...

48:23.520 --> 48:25.810
Add this and this.

48:26.170 --> 48:26.980
Oh, I see.

48:27.150 --> 48:29.910
You got it, Oumae-chan!

48:32.070 --> 48:34.070
OK, let's take a break.

48:35.030 --> 48:36.640
Shall we eat those?

48:36.640 --> 48:40.670
Huh? Um... they're for your mom.

48:41.330 --> 48:45.670
I had a feeling.
It was Kaori's idea, right?

48:45.920 --> 48:47.000
Well...

48:49.720 --> 48:52.880
Sorry, but my mom's
coming home late today.

48:53.760 --> 48:56.380
I'll give them to her though.

48:59.350 --> 49:00.770
Thank you.

49:01.040 --> 49:04.770
I'll go refresh your tea.

49:05.380 --> 49:06.850
I'll help.

49:09.070 --> 49:10.610
Pins and needles...

49:14.280 --> 49:16.610
We don't have any good snacks.

49:16.950 --> 49:18.250
Are cookies okay?

49:18.790 --> 49:21.270
Can I ask you something?

49:22.540 --> 49:25.580
Why did you offer to tutor me?

49:26.960 --> 49:31.090
I heard a rumor that your grades
were incredibly dismal.

49:31.280 --> 49:32.970
Who told you that?!

49:34.760 --> 49:35.880
Just kidding.

49:37.260 --> 49:39.600
I wanted to talk to you.

49:42.390 --> 49:43.430
Have you ever read this?

49:43.600 --> 49:44.600
EUPHONIUM

49:44.770 --> 49:46.890
Yes, I have a copy.

49:47.610 --> 49:50.440
Everyone reads it when they start playing.

49:51.990 --> 49:55.740
The author is a euphonium player
named Masakazu Shindo.

49:55.970 --> 49:57.180
WRITTEN BY MASAKAZU SHINDO

49:57.580 --> 50:00.520
He's famous. I have his CD too.

50:00.790 --> 50:02.250
He was my father.

50:04.790 --> 50:06.660
The tea's getting cold.

50:07.630 --> 50:09.510
Who cares about the tea?!

50:10.420 --> 50:11.900
Question time.

50:11.900 --> 50:15.820
Uh... you said he "was" your father. Why?

50:16.130 --> 50:21.040
Ah, isn't it obvious?
My parents got divorced.

50:23.100 --> 50:24.790
Tanaka is my mom's name.

50:25.140 --> 50:25.930
I see.

50:26.640 --> 50:32.150
They split up when I was two.
I don't remember him much.

50:33.980 --> 50:37.790
Have you seen your dad since?

50:39.330 --> 50:43.950
My mom doesn't want me to.

50:44.950 --> 50:50.130
You saw her at school.
She's a bit unstable.

50:50.550 --> 50:51.800
Unstable?

50:52.500 --> 50:56.170
She's super controlling,
and she gets hysterical.

50:57.050 --> 51:00.560
He must have gotten sick of that.

51:01.970 --> 51:05.720
But I don't hate her.

51:06.310 --> 51:11.690
She raised me as a single mom.
I know I owe her a lot.

51:14.480 --> 51:16.970
You say you don't hate her, but

51:17.320 --> 51:20.580
you actually do, right?

51:22.990 --> 51:24.830
It's not a matter of love or hate.

51:25.530 --> 51:28.750
My mother will always be my mother.

51:29.590 --> 51:33.590
I can't change that fact,
no matter how I struggle with it.

51:34.880 --> 51:37.720
I'm chained to it. For eternity.

51:40.010 --> 51:44.010
She has this ideal of happiness
etched in her mind.

51:44.180 --> 51:46.180
And concert band isn't part of it.

51:47.390 --> 51:48.400
From the beginning...

51:48.940 --> 51:51.360
Then why take up the euphonium?

51:51.940 --> 51:53.920
When I was in first grade,

51:54.400 --> 51:55.610
<i>I got a package.</i>

51:56.260 --> 51:57.520
TO ASUKA

51:57.700 --> 52:00.720
<i>A beat-up notebook,
a letter, and a euphonium.</i>

52:02.780 --> 52:08.540
<i>I heard someone at the local music store
used to play the euphonium.</i>

52:09.920 --> 52:13.210
<i>I tried playing and was pretty good at it.</i>

52:14.130 --> 52:16.880
<i>It made me so happy.</i>

52:18.050 --> 52:19.930
Sounds like a fairy tale.

52:22.050 --> 52:24.800
My mom was against it, of course.

52:25.890 --> 52:31.310
She tolerated it at first, but when she
saw I wasn't going to quit, we fought.

52:32.270 --> 52:36.900
In the end, we decided that I'd quit
the minute my grades began to suffer.

52:37.740 --> 52:38.610
That's why...

52:41.070 --> 52:44.140
I was desperate to continue
doing what I loved to do.

52:44.610 --> 52:47.450
So I always looked around me and thought,

52:48.580 --> 52:53.170
I'm not doing this for fun,
I'll just play for myself.

52:55.420 --> 52:57.190
It back-fired on me though.

52:59.340 --> 53:00.260
Look at this.

53:01.590 --> 53:03.630
The National Competition homepage...

53:04.630 --> 53:05.470
Ah, here it is.

53:05.700 --> 53:08.160
Masakazu Shindo.

53:08.600 --> 53:10.140
This lit a fire.

53:11.350 --> 53:13.770
I knew if we made it to Nationals,
he'd hear me play.

53:14.440 --> 53:15.270
So...

53:15.600 --> 53:19.050
I want to advance!

53:19.280 --> 53:21.800
I want Kitauji's sound
to resonate all over!

53:22.860 --> 53:26.820
It was self-serving though...
And look what happened.

53:27.490 --> 53:30.830
I guess God sees everything.

53:33.460 --> 53:38.440
Sorry, I didn't mean to ramble.
Shall we continue?

53:38.630 --> 53:42.780
I love your euphonium, Asuka-senpai!

53:43.510 --> 53:47.050
You were playing it by yourself
one morning at camp.

53:48.020 --> 53:49.890
When I heard you play that piece,

53:51.060 --> 53:53.710
I knew I loved your sound.

53:57.560 --> 54:00.990
That piece is by Masakazu Shindo.

54:02.320 --> 54:05.320
It was transcribed in the notebook
that came with the euphonium.

54:06.150 --> 54:07.150
Your dad's...

54:08.540 --> 54:14.200
Maybe I want you to hate that piece.

54:15.500 --> 54:17.540
Tear it to pieces.

54:18.550 --> 54:19.710
Why?

54:20.510 --> 54:22.260
I love that piece!

54:22.920 --> 54:27.510
It's so warm and gentle.

54:28.390 --> 54:32.100
I could listen to it forever!
I want to hear you play it now!

54:35.060 --> 54:36.520
Oumae-chan...

54:37.520 --> 54:39.860
You're so aggressive today.

54:43.010 --> 54:46.360
You're the one that's different today.

54:50.370 --> 54:52.790
Yeah, maybe so.

54:53.240 --> 54:53.950
Yes.

54:55.040 --> 54:57.080
Wanna go to the river?

54:57.700 --> 54:58.960
I feel like playing!

55:00.880 --> 55:01.550
Yes!

55:28.410 --> 55:30.600
Do you really want to hear it?

55:31.120 --> 55:31.740
Yes!

55:35.120 --> 55:38.500
You're just like a euphonium, Oumae-chan.

55:41.420 --> 55:46.130
I never thought of myself as a euphonium.

55:47.250 --> 55:50.760
So when I saw you, I was shocked.

55:51.510 --> 55:55.760
To see a girl who embodied the euphonium.

55:56.470 --> 55:57.640
Is that a complement?

55:58.360 --> 55:59.480
It sure is.

56:00.860 --> 56:05.360
Maybe that's why I wanted
to tell you about me.

56:08.450 --> 56:12.200
<i>I had never seen that smile before.</i>

56:12.370 --> 56:15.120
<i>It was so unlike Asuka-senpai.</i>

56:20.040 --> 56:21.230
So how was it?!

56:21.230 --> 56:22.360
How was what?

56:22.790 --> 56:24.690
Asuka-senpai!

56:24.690 --> 56:28.640
Oh... right. She was fine.

56:28.970 --> 56:32.010
But not ready to return to the band.

56:32.220 --> 56:35.640
I see... but her grades are so good.

56:35.800 --> 56:37.980
Why isn't her mom satisfied?

56:38.230 --> 56:43.400
Yeah! She's doing great
in school and band.

56:43.850 --> 56:46.650
Her mom is holding her back. I hate her!

56:46.980 --> 56:47.840
Calm down.

56:48.200 --> 56:51.090
But if you think about her future,

56:51.490 --> 56:57.030
quitting the band and focusing
on exams may be better for her.

56:57.200 --> 56:59.170
I know but...

56:59.670 --> 57:01.580
But still...

57:01.850 --> 57:05.750
I want to play with Asuka-senpai!

57:06.080 --> 57:07.040
Right?

57:19.230 --> 57:19.850
Something smells.

57:23.730 --> 57:26.270
What are you doing?

57:26.850 --> 57:28.780
Making miso soup.

57:33.030 --> 57:34.240
Hm? What's this?

57:34.900 --> 57:38.750
Dinner. Mom and Dad are going to be late.

57:38.960 --> 57:41.040
You're making dinner?!

57:41.620 --> 57:43.230
So what if I am?

57:44.540 --> 57:45.910
Did you make up?

57:46.870 --> 57:48.470
I plan to.

57:51.720 --> 57:53.300
What about you?

57:53.470 --> 57:55.820
We were let out early to study.

57:55.820 --> 57:58.560
I'm not usually home at this time of day.

57:59.270 --> 58:00.230
Right...

58:00.890 --> 58:02.890
Your timing sucks...

58:05.060 --> 58:05.770
I...

58:07.230 --> 58:10.780
I always avoided making
decisions for myself.

58:12.610 --> 58:16.280
I complained but went along
with whatever they decided.

58:18.080 --> 58:20.580
I thought that was doing my best.

58:21.450 --> 58:25.580
Listening to your parents and enduring.
I thought that was being mature.

58:28.300 --> 58:28.960
And?

58:29.800 --> 58:30.800
Go on.

58:32.840 --> 58:36.590
So you annoyed me.

58:37.300 --> 58:40.850
You were so carefree,
playing in the concert band.

58:43.600 --> 58:46.460
I was jealous of you.

58:47.520 --> 58:52.360
Your freedom. They let you do
whatever you wanted.

58:53.110 --> 58:56.650
But they totally favored you.

58:57.440 --> 59:00.450
They had low expectations
of me, that's all.

59:01.620 --> 59:03.120
Are you kidding me?

59:03.370 --> 59:04.330
No.

59:04.620 --> 59:07.540
Mom always praised you.

59:07.950 --> 59:10.380
And I was always sulking.

59:11.050 --> 59:14.780
I admit, she was proud of me.

59:15.960 --> 59:18.970
But I've decided to stop pretending.

59:21.350 --> 59:23.640
I tried to act like an adult
when I was only in high school.

59:23.890 --> 59:29.190
I gave up everything, and just endured.

59:29.650 --> 59:32.980
But that's meaningless.

59:35.230 --> 59:40.160
I'm ready to accept regret and failure

59:40.830 --> 59:42.330
<i>to walk my own path.</i>

59:44.870 --> 59:46.530
I wish I told them that.

59:47.910 --> 59:50.000
Even if they were against it.

59:50.500 --> 59:52.090
So no mistakes this time.

59:56.670 --> 59:58.820
You're moving out?

59:59.350 --> 59:59.890
Yeah.

01:00:00.390 --> 01:00:01.280
I see.

01:00:01.760 --> 01:00:02.550
Will you miss me?

01:00:03.680 --> 01:00:04.510
Not really.

01:00:05.010 --> 01:00:05.600
I see.

01:00:06.600 --> 01:00:09.610
I'll miss you a little. Just a little.

01:00:15.900 --> 01:00:19.620
I know. I'll go to Nationals
to hear you play.

01:00:19.870 --> 01:00:23.950
Huh? You'll come to hear me play?

01:00:24.410 --> 01:00:26.200
That's what I said.

01:00:29.790 --> 01:00:32.080
Come get me when Mom comes home.

01:00:32.420 --> 01:00:33.880
I'm going to take a nap.

01:00:35.630 --> 01:00:39.780
You should live your life
with no regrets too.

01:00:45.550 --> 01:00:46.140
Hot!

01:00:59.570 --> 01:01:02.240
Morning! No concert band today?

01:01:02.950 --> 01:01:03.660
Nope.

01:01:05.990 --> 01:01:07.070
Where's Mamiko?

01:01:07.910 --> 01:01:09.330
She went home this morning.

01:01:15.750 --> 01:01:16.750
I see.

01:01:36.170 --> 01:01:38.650
Again! Just once more!

01:01:38.950 --> 01:01:40.670
Oh, all right.

01:01:40.950 --> 01:01:42.890
I told you to be quiet.

01:01:44.610 --> 01:01:47.450
I was jealous of you.

01:01:48.150 --> 01:01:49.620
You really want to play?

01:01:50.120 --> 01:01:51.560
Yeah!

01:01:51.870 --> 01:01:53.830
I want to play with you!

01:02:12.060 --> 01:02:15.040
I'll miss you, too.

01:02:35.750 --> 01:02:36.560
OK.

01:02:37.080 --> 01:02:38.920
I told you!

01:02:40.380 --> 01:02:41.670
Asuka-senpai?

01:02:41.840 --> 01:02:47.450
Taki-Sensei said Natsuki's taking my place
and she agreed. End of story.

01:02:48.010 --> 01:02:50.390
Why rehash everything now?

01:02:50.560 --> 01:02:54.350
Nakagawa-san said
she really wants you to play.

01:02:54.770 --> 01:02:56.350
Of course she did.

01:02:57.180 --> 01:03:01.400
You think she'd actually say,
"Sure. I want to play?"

01:03:02.360 --> 01:03:03.110
But...

01:03:03.860 --> 01:03:04.530
But...

01:03:07.530 --> 01:03:10.200
I've already moved on.

01:03:11.120 --> 01:03:12.870
I'm focusing on my exams.

01:03:14.240 --> 01:03:14.950
Asuka...

01:03:15.580 --> 01:03:17.040
Are you sure?

01:03:18.080 --> 01:03:20.050
Is that really what you want?

01:03:21.920 --> 01:03:24.090
I told you from the beginning.

01:03:28.050 --> 01:03:31.620
I'll give you time to solve this problem.

01:03:35.310 --> 01:03:37.390
<i>Why is she lying like that?</i>

01:03:38.610 --> 01:03:41.880
<i>I know she wants to go to Nationals.</i>

01:03:42.730 --> 01:03:45.070
<i>I know she wants to play.</i>

01:03:51.780 --> 01:03:55.830
That's it for today.
Good luck on the test.

01:04:00.000 --> 01:04:02.090
Kumiko-chan, what about lunch?

01:04:03.090 --> 01:04:04.360
Go ahead.

01:04:13.430 --> 01:04:14.100
A freshman?

01:04:14.260 --> 01:04:15.100
- Who are you?

01:04:15.260 --> 01:04:19.580
Um, is Asuka-senpai... Asuka Tanaka here?

01:04:20.020 --> 01:04:21.610
Are you in the band?

01:04:21.940 --> 01:04:22.520
Yes.

01:04:23.250 --> 01:04:24.360
Asuka!

01:04:29.450 --> 01:04:32.950
That took guts, coming to my class.
Want a candy?

01:04:34.620 --> 01:04:35.990
Thank you.

01:04:36.870 --> 01:04:38.880
Someone gave it to me.

01:04:40.040 --> 01:04:42.960
How's this? So what is it?

01:04:43.670 --> 01:04:45.960
I need to talk to you.

01:04:46.290 --> 01:04:51.800
Did you fall in love with me
while you were at my house?

01:04:51.970 --> 01:04:52.830
No.

01:04:55.220 --> 01:04:56.140
I thought not.

01:04:57.680 --> 01:04:58.300
What is it?

01:04:58.810 --> 01:05:00.400
Please play at the competition.

01:05:01.690 --> 01:05:03.020
Is that it?

01:05:03.480 --> 01:05:04.060
Yes.

01:05:04.690 --> 01:05:06.150
The answer is no.

01:05:06.980 --> 01:05:10.660
The reason is because
it's better for the band.

01:05:10.990 --> 01:05:12.240
That's not true.

01:05:12.410 --> 01:05:13.350
Why?

01:05:13.820 --> 01:05:17.910
I can't go to practice. I don't even
know if I can go to the competition.

01:05:18.500 --> 01:05:20.750
I'll cause trouble for everyone.

01:05:21.370 --> 01:05:23.920
I wouldn't even want me there.

01:05:24.710 --> 01:05:27.330
You have a good reason.

01:05:28.210 --> 01:05:31.510
We all have our reasons.

01:05:32.260 --> 01:05:35.930
But everyone wants you to play.

01:05:36.220 --> 01:05:38.750
Everyone? Who's everyone?

01:05:39.850 --> 01:05:40.770
Well...

01:05:41.230 --> 01:05:45.770
Can you guarantee that
they're telling you the truth?

01:05:46.190 --> 01:05:47.020
Guarantee?

01:05:47.730 --> 01:05:49.970
That they want me to play.

01:05:50.360 --> 01:05:54.740
Of course they'll say
they want to play with me.

01:05:55.280 --> 01:05:58.030
That way no one gets hurt.

01:05:58.450 --> 01:06:00.210
No one will be criticized.

01:06:00.540 --> 01:06:04.120
But that doesn't mean
everyone feels that way.

01:06:05.210 --> 01:06:08.760
The bass section
and Natsuki-senpai feel that way.

01:06:08.940 --> 01:06:12.130
We all want you to play!

01:06:12.450 --> 01:06:14.280
How can you say that?

01:06:14.550 --> 01:06:15.530
I can!

01:06:19.770 --> 01:06:22.730
I can't believe you said that.

01:06:23.060 --> 01:06:24.060
Why can't I?

01:06:24.230 --> 01:06:25.580
You can, but...

01:06:26.770 --> 01:06:31.720
I wonder if you really know
everyone that well.

01:06:36.780 --> 01:06:40.910
You act like you care, but
you're afraid to hurt anyone and be hurt

01:06:41.080 --> 01:06:44.080
so you sit back and watch
from a safe distance.

01:06:44.950 --> 01:06:49.420
Who would bare their soul
to someone like that?

01:06:53.300 --> 01:06:57.760
You were so passionate just now.
What happened?

01:06:59.810 --> 01:07:02.680
It's better if I just fade out.

01:07:03.930 --> 01:07:07.600
Don't worry.
They'll forget me soon enough.

01:07:08.470 --> 01:07:10.610
Go to Nationals with a united front.

01:07:11.820 --> 01:07:15.480
The seniors are retiring
after that anyways.

01:07:15.680 --> 01:07:17.690
<i>I don't get that impression from her.</i>

01:07:17.930 --> 01:07:19.790
<i>It's better for the club.</i>

01:07:20.120 --> 01:07:23.830
<i>I want to play with Asuka-senpai!</i>

01:07:24.450 --> 01:07:26.330
So what?

01:07:26.830 --> 01:07:28.330
You're right!

01:07:29.020 --> 01:07:32.000
About the club, the competition,
everything!

01:07:32.170 --> 01:07:34.240
But I don't care about any of that!

01:07:34.550 --> 01:07:38.370
I just want to perform with you!
I want to!

01:07:39.060 --> 01:07:40.890
You're being childish--

01:07:41.060 --> 01:07:42.810
What's wrong with being childish?

01:07:43.160 --> 01:07:45.620
Why do you try to act so mature?

01:07:45.620 --> 01:07:50.190
As if you know all the answers?
As if you're the only special one?

01:07:50.880 --> 01:07:53.650
You're just a high school student too!

01:07:54.070 --> 01:07:56.730
What's so good about that?

01:07:57.630 --> 01:08:01.330
You want your dad to hear you play, right?

01:08:01.640 --> 01:08:04.330
You want to go to Nationals!

01:08:04.660 --> 01:08:08.200
How can you pretend that wasn't real?

01:08:09.040 --> 01:08:13.840
Giving up, compromising, enduring!
That's just selfish!

01:08:14.420 --> 01:08:15.340
It's not right...

01:08:18.500 --> 01:08:23.220
We're all waiting for you...
Don't give up.

01:08:24.600 --> 01:08:29.690
Don't choose a path
that you know you'll regret.

01:08:33.020 --> 01:08:36.840
Please don't give up
until you've given it your all!

01:08:37.360 --> 01:08:40.030
I want you to perform at Nationals!

01:08:40.530 --> 01:08:43.200
I want you to play in that hall!

01:08:43.530 --> 01:08:46.070
I want to hear you play the euphonium!

01:08:53.210 --> 01:08:56.280
You should see your face. It's a mess.

01:08:56.540 --> 01:08:58.460
But.. but...

01:09:00.550 --> 01:09:03.260
You're so emotional.
What's gotten into you?

01:09:03.550 --> 01:09:04.490
But...

01:09:04.760 --> 01:09:07.000
But I'm glad.

01:09:08.260 --> 01:09:09.400
Really glad.

01:09:10.600 --> 01:09:11.560
Senpai?

01:09:11.770 --> 01:09:12.480
Yes?

01:09:12.770 --> 01:09:14.810
Can I see your face?

01:09:14.980 --> 01:09:15.670
No.

01:09:16.400 --> 01:09:18.480
If you look, I'll curse you
'til the end of time.

01:09:22.240 --> 01:09:23.240
Asuka!

01:09:26.950 --> 01:09:29.750
Asuka, Ikeda-Sensei is calling you.

01:09:30.290 --> 01:09:32.620
About the mock exam.

01:09:33.250 --> 01:09:36.170
Mock exam? Sorry! I have to go.

01:09:43.300 --> 01:09:46.430
Haruka! Did you hear about the mock exam?

01:09:47.970 --> 01:09:48.850
Excuse me.

01:09:54.100 --> 01:09:55.690
Natsuki! Good news!

01:09:55.850 --> 01:09:56.850
What is it?

01:09:57.020 --> 01:09:58.310
Asuka-senpai!

01:10:27.380 --> 01:10:30.480
OK, we'll start in five minutes.

01:10:31.180 --> 01:10:32.060
Seriously?

01:10:34.060 --> 01:10:35.390
See you later.

01:10:36.810 --> 01:10:38.020
Practice is starting.

01:10:38.180 --> 01:10:40.570
Haven't you heard?

01:10:40.990 --> 01:10:43.030
Asuka-senpai is so mean.

01:10:43.990 --> 01:10:45.320
Asuka-senpai?

01:10:49.160 --> 01:10:51.160
Sorry I'm late.

01:10:56.660 --> 01:10:58.160
What's going on?

01:10:58.660 --> 01:11:02.880
Asuka-senpai was in the top 30
nationwide on the mock exam.

01:11:03.550 --> 01:11:07.840
She used that as leverage
to convince her mom.

01:11:09.680 --> 01:11:11.060
Sorry, Natsuki.

01:11:11.390 --> 01:11:13.020
Don't apologize to me.

01:11:13.850 --> 01:11:17.180
I was waiting for you to come back.

01:11:28.870 --> 01:11:29.950
Welcome back.

01:11:31.870 --> 01:11:32.870
I'm back.

01:12:02.400 --> 01:12:04.320
This is our last practice.

01:12:05.230 --> 01:12:08.730
Did you contact your dad?

01:12:10.120 --> 01:12:11.220
No way.

01:12:12.410 --> 01:12:13.490
I see.

01:12:14.580 --> 01:12:16.660
Shall we begin?

01:12:16.990 --> 01:12:18.620
Please take care of us.

01:12:47.610 --> 01:12:49.030
<i>We're here at Nationals.</i>

01:12:50.450 --> 01:12:53.620
<i>Our hearts are full
of so many different emotions.</i>

01:12:54.820 --> 01:12:57.490
<i>This may be the first time
I'm playing feeling this way.</i>

01:12:59.880 --> 01:13:03.630
<i>I want our sound to resonate in this hall.</i>

01:13:05.110 --> 01:13:07.960
<i>I want our sound to reach them!</i>

01:13:11.680 --> 01:13:15.200
OK, everyone. Got your ribbons on?

01:13:15.470 --> 01:13:17.300
Where's my ribbon?

01:13:17.680 --> 01:13:18.980
It's on your arm.

01:13:19.350 --> 01:13:21.850
Percussions, watch your route.

01:13:22.020 --> 01:13:22.690
Yes!

01:13:32.070 --> 01:13:35.990
This is it. The day of our performance.

01:13:37.240 --> 01:13:42.900
We set our sights on Nationals
this spring. Now we're here.

01:13:43.500 --> 01:13:47.330
I won't tell you not to worry
about the outcome.

01:13:47.540 --> 01:13:51.010
But it's important to
play without any regrets.

01:13:52.220 --> 01:13:53.220
Especially the seniors.

01:13:53.680 --> 01:13:54.340
Yes!

01:13:55.090 --> 01:14:00.600
This will be your final performance.
Leave everything on this stage.

01:14:01.020 --> 01:14:01.730
Yes!

01:14:01.920 --> 01:14:04.190
May I say something?

01:14:05.020 --> 01:14:06.850
Of course. Go ahead.

01:14:09.570 --> 01:14:10.900
This is it.

01:14:12.030 --> 01:14:15.070
I won't say anything negative today.

01:14:16.240 --> 01:14:20.210
I'm excited from the bottom of my heart.

01:14:21.250 --> 01:14:23.580
Let's do our best and win gold!

01:14:23.900 --> 01:14:24.620
Yes!

01:14:25.250 --> 01:14:26.960
Vice President Asuka!

01:14:32.090 --> 01:14:37.720
I'm sorry I caused so much anxiety
on this journey to Nationals.

01:14:38.470 --> 01:14:42.560
I'm here today thanks to all of you.

01:14:43.140 --> 01:14:43.890
Thank you.

01:14:44.930 --> 01:14:49.490
Let's play the best music
we've ever played.

01:14:50.280 --> 01:14:53.070
And finish with a smile!

01:14:53.400 --> 01:14:54.070
Yes!

01:14:56.570 --> 01:14:59.140
Thank you for listening!

01:14:59.830 --> 01:15:00.580
Haruka!

01:15:01.080 --> 01:15:01.910
All right!

01:15:03.290 --> 01:15:05.160
Let's cheer, everybody.

01:15:05.830 --> 01:15:08.080
Kitauji, go!

01:15:19.930 --> 01:15:20.970
Asuka-senpai.

01:15:23.520 --> 01:15:27.310
My sister is here today.

01:15:37.150 --> 01:15:38.780
Then I'll have to do my very best.

01:15:40.540 --> 01:15:41.700
You too, Kumiko.

01:15:42.870 --> 01:15:43.790
Yes.

01:15:43.950 --> 01:15:46.200
Let's go, Kitauji.

01:15:47.870 --> 01:15:48.450
Let's go!

01:15:48.790 --> 01:15:49.480
Yes.

01:15:50.380 --> 01:15:56.170
<i>Representing Kansai is
Kitauji High School led by...</i>

01:17:38.220 --> 01:17:40.380
LET'S DO IT!

01:19:59.820 --> 01:20:02.650
THIS IS OUR LAST CONCERT! LET'S ENJOY IT!

01:20:35.850 --> 01:20:38.990
FLY, KITAUJI!

01:21:45.340 --> 01:21:48.470
NATIONALS

01:23:44.850 --> 01:23:48.460
We have time until
the results are announced.

01:23:48.680 --> 01:23:50.780
Maybe I'll go to the café.

01:23:51.280 --> 01:23:52.860
I'll go with you.

01:23:53.480 --> 01:23:56.970
Neither of you are staying
to listen to the other bands?

01:23:56.970 --> 01:23:57.940
Nope.

01:23:58.430 --> 01:24:00.660
We're no longer president and
vice president anyway.

01:24:02.370 --> 01:24:03.330
Right.

01:24:04.040 --> 01:24:07.870
Then maybe I'll go too.

01:24:08.040 --> 01:24:08.990
Let's go!

01:24:10.110 --> 01:24:14.860
OK! Let's devour a
chocolate banana sundae.

01:24:15.170 --> 01:24:17.360
Jumbo chocolate banana sundae!

01:24:17.670 --> 01:24:18.460
Is there such a thing?

01:24:18.630 --> 01:24:20.720
I'll ask them to make one.

01:24:36.650 --> 01:24:41.760
Now for the results of
the high school division.

01:24:41.760 --> 01:24:42.890
This is it.

01:24:44.890 --> 01:24:47.900
Number 1, Gigan Commercial High School,

01:24:47.900 --> 01:24:48.910
Silver medal.

01:24:52.540 --> 01:24:55.880
I award you the silver medal.

01:24:57.500 --> 01:24:59.720
Number 2, Katashiki High School,

01:25:00.260 --> 01:25:01.350
Gold medal.

01:25:05.890 --> 01:25:09.350
Number 3, Kitauji High School.

01:25:27.120 --> 01:25:30.940
Why the sad faces? Smile!

01:25:31.420 --> 01:25:33.210
We're trying, but...

01:25:33.440 --> 01:25:34.750
AWARD

01:25:34.940 --> 01:25:36.530
BRONZE MEDAL

01:25:42.590 --> 01:25:44.470
We're sorry, senpai.

01:25:44.800 --> 01:25:49.500
Why are you apologizing?
We gave it our best shot.

01:25:50.230 --> 01:25:53.600
We'll win gold next year.

01:25:55.400 --> 01:25:56.130
Yes.

01:25:56.130 --> 01:26:00.010
What an amazing performance!
It brought tears to my eyes!

01:26:00.010 --> 01:26:01.570
It was wonderful.

01:26:01.760 --> 01:26:05.640
- Ogasawara! You worked so hard!
- I can't breathe!

01:26:05.820 --> 01:26:07.390
We're counting on you next year.

01:26:08.110 --> 01:26:08.740
Yes.

01:26:15.960 --> 01:26:16.830
What's up?

01:26:17.080 --> 01:26:18.250
Nothing.

01:26:19.000 --> 01:26:21.840
Tanaka-san and Kumiko-san,
I was looking for you.

01:26:22.300 --> 01:26:25.260
I have something to tell you.

01:26:26.590 --> 01:26:30.270
Do you know who Masakazu Shindo is?

01:26:31.810 --> 01:26:33.810
He's one of the judges today.

01:26:34.140 --> 01:26:37.050
Yes... he's a euphonium player.

01:26:37.850 --> 01:26:40.780
I just ran into him in the hallway, and

01:26:40.990 --> 01:26:44.450
he had a message
for our euphonium players.

01:26:45.150 --> 01:26:46.780
A message?

01:26:47.110 --> 01:26:47.700
Yes.

01:26:50.000 --> 01:26:54.830
"I'm glad you kept it up.
Your sound was beautiful."

01:27:02.300 --> 01:27:04.280
Do either of you know him?

01:27:04.470 --> 01:27:06.280
Yes... a little.

01:27:09.050 --> 01:27:11.910
Yes! He liked my sound!

01:27:12.680 --> 01:27:14.640
I'm so happy for you.

01:27:29.030 --> 01:27:29.850
Dad.

01:27:29.850 --> 01:27:30.660
TO ASUKA

01:27:44.710 --> 01:27:47.340
We seniors are retiring as of today.

01:27:48.010 --> 01:27:53.060
Thank you for letting me
be your president.

01:27:53.850 --> 01:27:57.100
We went through
a lot of hardships this year.

01:27:58.100 --> 01:28:00.530
And a lot of uncertainty...

01:28:00.900 --> 01:28:04.360
But through it all,
I was happy playing with you.

01:28:09.230 --> 01:28:12.290
I'll speak on behalf
of our emotional president.

01:28:13.910 --> 01:28:17.700
To be honest, I have nothing to say
about today's performance.

01:28:18.450 --> 01:28:21.130
Kitauji's sound resonated
throughout Japan.

01:28:22.090 --> 01:28:24.130
We gave it everything we had.

01:28:24.960 --> 01:28:26.920
Thank you for your hard work.

01:28:28.460 --> 01:28:33.430
Now the seniors are retiring.
Juniors, it's up to you.

01:28:33.930 --> 01:28:35.600
That makes me really nervous.

01:28:38.100 --> 01:28:43.770
As you know, I'm not one to beat
around the bush, so I'll just say it.

01:28:44.440 --> 01:28:47.610
I'm not happy with the outcome today.

01:28:48.770 --> 01:28:51.910
But this is it for us seniors.

01:28:53.120 --> 01:28:55.580
We'll bear it, but you don't have to.

01:28:57.740 --> 01:29:01.500
You guys win gold next year!

01:29:02.920 --> 01:29:06.250
That's my final order to you as your
vice president. Understood?

01:29:06.670 --> 01:29:07.420
Yes!

01:29:08.590 --> 01:29:11.510
I won't forget that!

01:29:11.760 --> 01:29:14.200
I'll come visit you every day.

01:29:14.600 --> 01:29:16.640
Senpai, please don't...

01:29:16.800 --> 01:29:19.080
Huh? Why not?

01:29:20.460 --> 01:29:21.310
Mamiko!

01:29:23.150 --> 01:29:23.880
Kumiko...

01:29:27.940 --> 01:29:28.810
Oumae-san?

01:29:31.950 --> 01:29:32.620
Asuka?

01:29:34.280 --> 01:29:36.450
We'll scold her later.

01:29:54.050 --> 01:29:54.970
Welcome back.

01:29:55.640 --> 01:29:57.010
Asuka-senpai.

01:29:58.390 --> 01:30:00.520
So? Did you see her?

01:30:03.020 --> 01:30:05.150
Yes, I did.

01:30:06.900 --> 01:30:10.410
I told her exactly how I felt.

01:30:22.980 --> 01:30:23.710
I see.

01:30:28.830 --> 01:30:31.720
Let's go then. Everyone's waiting.

01:30:31.880 --> 01:30:33.840
Ah! I'm sorry!

01:30:34.340 --> 01:30:35.680
You'll get it later.

01:30:37.220 --> 01:30:38.680
Oh yeah, Oumae-chan?

01:30:39.010 --> 01:30:39.680
Yes?

01:30:43.230 --> 01:30:45.270
Do you like the euphonium?

01:30:48.600 --> 01:30:50.570
Yes, I do!

01:30:55.070 --> 01:30:55.860
Me too!

01:31:07.040 --> 01:31:08.870
<i>To my sister,</i>

01:31:10.300 --> 01:31:15.120
<i>It's a little embarrassing
writing letters to each other.</i>

01:31:17.760 --> 01:31:20.390
<i>It's February and getting colder.</i>

01:31:21.500 --> 01:31:23.730
<i>Nothing much new here.</i>

01:31:24.890 --> 01:31:27.560
<i>I'm studying and practicing every day.</i>

01:31:29.060 --> 01:31:33.110
<i>Mom seems worried
about my future already...</i>

01:31:34.260 --> 01:31:34.940
CONGRATULATIONS

01:31:35.110 --> 01:31:39.110
<i>But I want to go to Nationals again,
and win gold this time.</i>

01:31:40.450 --> 01:31:41.660
<i>No regrets.</i>

01:31:43.080 --> 01:31:45.250
<i>Just like you said.</i>

01:31:57.870 --> 01:32:04.120
FAREWELL SENIORS

01:32:09.250 --> 01:32:11.760
GRADUATION CEREMONY

01:32:18.610 --> 01:32:22.370
Valedictorian and Class Representative
Asuka Tanaka.

01:32:23.040 --> 01:32:23.660
Yes!

01:32:27.950 --> 01:32:28.950
Graduates,

01:32:29.330 --> 01:32:33.960
the warmth and light of
spring can be felt in the air.

01:32:36.820 --> 01:32:39.200
Thank you, Taki-Sensei.

01:32:39.670 --> 01:32:41.200
Good luck, senpai!

01:32:41.640 --> 01:32:42.720
You too!

01:32:43.140 --> 01:32:44.560
You'll be college students soon.

01:32:44.970 --> 01:32:45.660
Yes!

01:32:47.350 --> 01:32:47.970
Here!

01:32:48.970 --> 01:32:52.190
What will I do without you?

01:32:52.820 --> 01:32:54.130
What are you saying?

01:32:55.900 --> 01:32:57.650
We'll come to watch your performances.

01:32:59.230 --> 01:33:02.140
You're the president now. Be strong!

01:33:23.600 --> 01:33:27.850
Welcome to Kitauji High School, freshmen!

01:33:30.400 --> 01:33:33.440
Congratulations on
your entrance to high school!

01:33:40.410 --> 01:33:43.030
Hey, Oumae-chan!

01:33:44.120 --> 01:33:46.240
What are you doing here?

01:33:49.140 --> 01:33:51.710
What are you doing here?

01:33:52.210 --> 01:33:54.710
I don't really like these things.

01:33:55.210 --> 01:33:58.080
Congratulations on your graduation.

01:33:58.460 --> 01:34:01.890
I told you, I don't like these things.

01:34:02.720 --> 01:34:04.800
Is something wrong?

01:34:05.140 --> 01:34:07.720
I wanted to tell you something.

01:34:08.090 --> 01:34:10.810
Me? You were looking for me?

01:34:11.560 --> 01:34:12.210
Yes.

01:34:12.210 --> 01:34:15.150
What is it? Are you in love?

01:34:15.730 --> 01:34:16.650
Yes.

01:34:20.240 --> 01:34:21.070
Are you serious?

01:34:21.740 --> 01:34:24.780
We weren't compatible at first.

01:34:25.610 --> 01:34:29.140
But you were a senior and
we both played the euphonium...

01:34:29.450 --> 01:34:32.900
I didn't think you were
easy to get along with.

01:34:33.290 --> 01:34:36.120
I may have even disliked you.

01:34:40.000 --> 01:34:41.760
Is that what you wanted to say?

01:34:42.010 --> 01:34:43.090
Is that weird?

01:34:43.260 --> 01:34:44.470
Well, sure.

01:34:45.010 --> 01:34:47.930
Because I knew all along.

01:34:48.120 --> 01:34:49.580
You don't know anything!

01:34:50.940 --> 01:34:53.940
Because I love you now.

01:34:58.480 --> 01:35:01.820
You never show anyone how you really feel.

01:35:02.200 --> 01:35:04.490
I felt like you looked down on me.

01:35:05.110 --> 01:35:07.650
You said you didn't care
about the competition.

01:35:08.650 --> 01:35:11.960
But... I'll miss you.

01:35:13.120 --> 01:35:16.540
I want to hear you play the euphonium.

01:35:17.500 --> 01:35:21.860
I want to play the euphonium like you.

01:35:23.010 --> 01:35:24.470
Is that what you wanted to tell me?

01:35:31.520 --> 01:35:32.520
For you.

01:35:35.310 --> 01:35:37.890
This is your dad's...

01:35:39.310 --> 01:35:41.820
I don't need it anymore.

01:35:44.860 --> 01:35:49.360
It's your turn to share this piece
with the younger members.

01:35:50.580 --> 01:35:53.040
I don't want to say good-bye.

01:35:56.330 --> 01:35:57.330
Then I won't.

01:36:15.850 --> 01:36:16.720
See you!

01:36:18.220 --> 01:36:18.930
Yes!

01:36:50.430 --> 01:36:54.390
<i>Asuka-senpai played
that piece for me once.</i>

01:36:55.970 --> 01:37:00.940
<i>But it was only then
that I learned the title.</i>

01:37:01.170 --> 01:37:02.920
SOUND! EUPHONIUM

01:37:07.070 --> 01:37:08.070
Kumiko!

01:37:10.620 --> 01:37:12.120
There you are.

01:37:13.080 --> 01:37:15.120
Ensemble practice this afternoon!

01:37:16.080 --> 01:37:17.910
Sorry! I'm coming!

01:37:20.630 --> 01:37:22.960
<i>"Sound! Euphonium."</i>

01:37:25.460 --> 01:37:30.130
<i>I'll never forget the warmth
of that sound.</i>

01:37:30.290 --> 01:37:36.600
SOUND! EUPHONIUM
